TITLE:: Ptransduce
SUMMARY:: Stateful zero, one or many outputs per input
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pscan, Classes/Pcollect, Classes/Pselect

DESCRIPTION::
Calls function(state, input, index, inval) for each source item. Return an Event containing state and an optional emit collection. Stop true emits the supplied items and ends; returning nil ends immediately. Only natural source termination invokes flush, once. See link::Reference/Patternarium-Protocols::. Output collection items are yielded directly, including Arrays and Events. Nil items are rejected. State is not copied. Memory depends on user state and the current emission collection. A transition that never emits can consume arbitrarily many source items in one next call.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: pattern
Source Pattern, streamed with the latest inval.
ARGUMENT:: initial
State evaluated once with value(inval). Use a Function for fresh mutable state.
ARGUMENT:: function
Function returning a validated step Event or nil. Index starts at zero.
ARGUMENT:: flush
Optional Function called with state, number of consumed items and latest inval on natural termination. Uses the same result protocol.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns the constructor arguments for archive reconstruction.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Runs the stream protocol and returns the latest inval on termination.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Ptransduce(Pseq([1, 2, 3]), 0, { |s, x| (state: s + x, emit: [s + x]) }).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Ptransduce / Value stream
var values = {
Ptransduce(Pseq([1, 2, 3]), 0, { |s, x| (state: s + x, emit: [s + x]) }).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: x*3, dur: 0.16, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Musical example
Load the example instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments:: first, then evaluate this block.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \fmPiano, \degree, Ptransduce(Pseq([0, 2, 4, 5]), 0, { |s, x| (state: x, emit: [x, x + 1, x]) }), \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Debouncing
code::
Ptransduce(Pseq([0, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0]), (last: -1, n: 0), { |s, x|
    var n = if(x == s[\last]) { s[\n] + 1 } { 1 };
    (state: (last: x, n: n), emit: if(n == 2) { [x] } { [] })
}).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Ptransduce / Debouncing
var values = {
Ptransduce(Pseq([0, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0]), (last: -1, n: 0), { |s, x|
    var n = if(x == s[\last]) { s[\n] + 1 } { 1 };
    (state: (last: x, n: n), emit: if(n == 2) { [x] } { [] })
}).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: x*3, dur: 0.16, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Hysteresis
code::
Ptransduce(Pseq([0.2, 0.6, 0.9, 0.5, 0.1]), 0, { |s, x|
    var next = if(x > 0.8) { 1 } { if(x < 0.3) { 0 } { s } };
    (state: next, emit: [next])
}).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Ptransduce / Hysteresis
var values = {
Ptransduce(Pseq([0.2, 0.6, 0.9, 0.5, 0.1]), 0, { |s, x|
    var next = if(x > 0.8) { 1 } { if(x < 0.3) { 0 } { s } };
    (state: next, emit: [next])
}).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: x*3, dur: 0.16, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Symbolic token parsing
code::
Ptransduce(Pseq([\a, \b, \space, \c, \space]), [], { |s, x|
    if(x == \space) { (state: [], emit: [s]) } { (state: s.add(x), emit: []) }
}).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Ptransduce / Symbolic token parsing
var values = {
Ptransduce(Pseq([\a, \b, \space, \c, \space]), [], { |s, x|
    if(x == \space) { (state: [], emit: [s]) } { (state: s.add(x), emit: []) }
}).asStream.all;
}.value;
var tones = (a: 0, b: 2, c: 4, d: 7, x: 9, y: 11, tonic: [0,2,4], subdominant: [3,5,7], dominant: [4,6,8], dark: 0, warm: 2, bright: 7, kick: -7, snare: 0, hat: 14, intro: 0, verse: 2, chorus: 4, bridge: 7, outro: 0, quiet: 0, medium: 2, loud: 4), labels;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: x.collect { |v| if(v.isNumber) { v } { tones[v] ? 0 } }, dur: 0.35, amp: 0.05)
}.play;
)
::

